although the familiar formula is largely  intact pokemon sword and shield at a ton  of new features that shake up the  experience whether you're a beginner or  a veteran here are some useful tidbits  to keep in mind as you're exploring the  gallery region  [Music]  catching Pokemon works the same as it  always has but the types of Pokemon you  can find in the wild area can vary due  to location and most importantly whether  the wild area is divided into several  regions and weather will change from  region to region each day the types of  weather you encounter include rain  sandstorms and harsh sunlight and the  terrain types from Sun and Moon from  what we can tell the weather changes  every day so you'll want to revisit the  wild area often fortunately you don't  need to visit the wild area every time  you want to check the weather if you  open a town map you can hover over  different zones to see what the climate  is like or you can toggle weather on  with the plus button  [Music]  when you take your first steps in the  wild area you will most likely encounter  an Onix to the left what's odd about  this Onix is that it's off on its own  outside the tall grass in Pokemon sword  and shield if you see a pokemon  wandering around outside the grass that  usually means it's a high level Pokemon  nothing is stopping you from battling  these Pokemon right away but I would  advise caution if you aren't careful  many of these Pokemon can chew through  your party in a few moves  even if you do manage to whittle down  their HP you won't be able to catch them  until you have enough badges before you  venture out into the wild area we  recommend taking some polka dolls along  with you because these allow you to flee  without fail once you have a few gym  badges you'll want to return to the wild  area frequently so you can find and  catch these rare and powerful Pokemon  without digging into spoilers there are  some exciting and unexpected Pokemon you  can find in the wild area  Pokemon's sergeant shield also adds  camping before you get to the wild area  your mum will give you a camping set  this allows you to set up a tent play  with your Pokemon and cook curry  apart from being a heartwarming  diversion there are in-game benefits to  camping playing with your Pokemon will  strengthen your bond and net them some  experience points and if you need a  break from catching and battling then  maybe it's time to give your Pokemon a  well-earned rest  the highlight of the wild area are their  raid battles these battles allow you and  three other trainers both NPCs and real  players to battle and catch a Dynomax  Pokemon to initiate one of these you'll  need to find a den with a beam of light  shooting out of the ground once you and  your team knock out the Pokemon every  player is given one chance to catch it  from what we can tell the odds of  catching a red pokemon are fairly high  fortunately even if you don't catch the  Dynomax Pokemon you will get a bunch of  rewards including rare candies and XP  candies among other things early raid  battles can be completed by yourself  however they do get much tougher when  you start seeing four or five star raids  pop up we recommend finding a few  buddies with high-level Pokemon to join  you as these battles can require a fair  bit of coordination and preparation  [Music]  as you inspect Pokemon dens in the wild  area you will collect a currency called  Watts Watts can be traded to NPCs 40 ARS  which are basically single-use TMS  retro-style  and wishing pieces throw a wishing piece  into an empty den and voila a Pokemon  will appear and you can do a max raid  even if there's no beam of light  if you see a Pokemon with a yellowish  glow around it catch it right away it's  not shiny it's more powerful than normal  and that glow means it's generating  watts catching or defeating this Pokemon  will net you some watts but catching it  is better because these pokemon also  have some perfect stats  [Music]  while you can access your Pokemon boxes  from anywhere you'll want to hit up the  roto me PC in any pokemon center from  time to time this is the only way you  can access Pokemon jobs assignments you  can send your Pokemon on for experience  points and other minor rewards most of  these jobs are dependent on type like  sending a certain number of grass type  Pokemon to help some people out all you  need to do is pick the Pokemon decide  how long you want them gone and move on  with your day it's a great way to put  your box Pokemon to use so they don't  seem so lonely in there  Pokemon's sword and shield don't have  random encounters instead most Pokemon  walk around the overworld like they did  in let's go Pikachu and Eevee  however there are some Pokemon that will  pop up as an exclamation point in the  tall grass  these aren't totally random because you  have to walk up to them to interact with  them and start a battle but the Pokemon  you get will be random and there are  some Pokemon that can only be found  hidden in the tall grass like this those  are just a few tips to keep in mind as  you explore Galler  if you're still unsure which version to  pick up check out our video outlining  the key differences between sword and  shield for more Pokemon stay tuned to  game spot  [Music]  you
 

